+## When beforeSession throws
+
+- A throw from `beforeSession` reaches the same `catch` and `finally` as any other failure in the turn: the original error still rejects the caller, `onError` fires with the session and that error, and `afterSession` runs after it ([validated by: runs onError then afterSession and still rejects when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L42)).
+- `afterSession` running after a failed `beforeSession` sees a session the turn never started — the provider was never consulted and the entries are exactly what the caller passed in — so a cleanup hook must tolerate a session it never set up rather than assuming its own allocation happened ([validated by: hands afterSession a session the turn never started](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L79)).
+
 ## Engine startup
 
 - The engine's `start()` method rejects the returned promise when it cannot bind the configured port, rather than emitting an unhandled error event that would take the process down ([validated by: rejects instead of taking the process down with an unhandled error event](../../src/config.test.ts#L174)).
 
